---
/**
 * AssessmentBand — the home page's door into the AI Fit Assessment.
 *
 * WHY IT EXISTS. The assessment shipped on 2026-09-03 with four inbound links,
 * and not one of them was on the home page: the footer, the Services drop-down,
 * the mobile Menu sheet, and one panel on /services/. A paid offer reachable
 * only from a menu is a paid offer most visitors never learn about.
 *
 * WHY IT SITS AFTER Offers AND NOT NEAR THE TOP. index.astro records the page
 * order as load-bearing, and the free check holds the slot straight after the
 * opener because it is the one thing on the page a stranger can act on. Putting
 * a paid item above it would take the reader out of the funnel at the exact
 * point it is meant to pull them in. The reader who reaches this band has
 * already been shown the free check and the three things that get built, which
 * is the right moment to say "and if you cannot tell which of those you need".
 *
 * IT NAMES NO FIGURE, AND THAT IS A RULE RATHER THAN A STYLE CHOICE. The price
 * and the credit are one statement — the fee WITHOUT the credit is a worse offer
 * than the one being sold — and scripts/verify-assessment.mjs requires them
 * within 400 characters of each other wherever the price appears. This band has
 * no room for the pair, so it carries neither. The page it opens carries both.
 *
 * ONE HEADING, ONE PARAGRAPH, ONE BUTTON. Headroom on a 390px phone is thin and
 * this page's whole history is growing back. Measure with
 * `node scripts/measure-pages.mjs` before adding a second sentence.
 */
import Section from '../Section.astro';
---
<Section tone="canvas">
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between">
    <div class="max-w-xl">
      <p class="mono-label">If you cannot tell which of those you need</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-3xl">
        Everyone says you should be using AI. Nobody says where.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        So I come out, watch an hour of the work actually happening, and write you a list of what is
        worth building — in order, with a number beside each line. If the honest answer is that no
        software fixes it, the document says that, and you still keep the document.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="shrink-0">
      <a href="/ai-fit/" class="btn btn-primary">The AI Fit Assessment →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Section>
